From 05a104a4c2b79ad0589dc14e7674e29f5e0f1b97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slopdealer <326519127+slopdealer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:18:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 39/49] Red team fix 8: collected terminal output keeps the
 message boundaries

Output for a regular file is collected and written in one call. When that
call failed, the remainder was cut by lines: a write that stopped exactly at
the end of a message cost the next message, which stock writes, and a message
of several lines lost only one line where stock gives up the message.

The batch now carries the offset at which each message ends, from Print and
from the output writer (stock prints the complete lines of one Write as one
message). After a failed write the message in which it stopped is given up
and every later message is written once on its own. A write that stopped
exactly between two messages stopped in none, so the next one is written;
when that write repeats the reported error it is the same failure (a disk
that is full fails the next message with nothing written, in stock too) and
is reported once.

Tests: TestBatchErrorAtMessageBoundary (seat 3 finding 3, carried in; the
call passes the message ends) fails before and passes after;
TestBatchErrorFollowsMessagesNotLines, TestBatchOnFullDiskFollowsMessages and
TestOutputWriterKeepsMessageOfOneWrite compare file content and reports with
stock's one write per message for every failing byte.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
